Overview
This project delivers a systematic, production-grade framework for evaluating and selecting open-source large language models (LLMs) for AIOps fine-tuning. The evaluation process is modular,hardware-aware, and supports multi-metric scoring to ensure the best model is chosen fordownstream QLORA fine-tuning.
Key Features
Multi-metric scoring:
Code quality, logic, entity extraction, hallucination, and format strictness
Hardware-aware quantization:
4-bit/8-bit/FP16 based on available VRAM
Incremental, modular datasets:
Task-specific evaluation for AIOps (log parsing, code gen,reasoning, instruction)
Deterministic evaluation:
Reproducible results (temperature=0, seed=42)
QLORA pilot workflow:
For final model selection
